Subject: [PATCH] scripts/package/wb: add sa02m / sa02m-rt flavours

Wiren Board Debian kernel build system uses `scripts/package/wb/version.sh`
to dispatch on `$KERNEL_FLAVOUR` (wb2/wb6/wb7/...). Add two new flavours so
`make -f wb.mk deb KERNEL_FLAVOUR=sa02m` produces `linux-image-sa02m` for
ЦИНТРОН SA-02м.

  - sa02m    : baseline SMP kernel (defconfig = sa02m_defconfig)
  - sa02m-rt : PREEMPT_RT kernel  (defconfig = sa02m_rt_defconfig)

Both flavours use armhf toolchain (`arm-linux-gnueabihf-`) — matches WB7.

Applied by [../apply.sh](../apply.sh) into a wirenboard/linux checkout.

Signed-off-by: ЦИНТРОН <dev@cyntron.ru>

diff --git a/scripts/package/wb/version.sh b/scripts/package/wb/version.sh
index xxxxxxxxx..yyyyyyyyy 100755
--- a/scripts/package/wb/version.sh
+++ b/scripts/package/wb/version.sh
@@ -66,9 +66,19 @@ setup_kernel_vars() {
 			BOOTLET_DEPS=
 			KDEB_WBDESC="Wiren Board 7 (factory bootlet)"
 			;;
+		sa02m)
+			DEBARCH=armhf
+			KERNEL_DEFCONFIG=sa02m_defconfig
+			KDEB_WBDESC="Cyntron SA-02m (Allwinner A40i)"
+			;;
+		sa02m-rt)
+			DEBARCH=armhf
+			KERNEL_DEFCONFIG=sa02m_defconfig
+			KDEB_WBDESC="Cyntron SA-02m (Allwinner A40i, PREEMPT_RT)"
+			;;
 		*)
-			echo "Unsupported KERNEL_FLAVOUR, please specify one of: wb2, wb6, wb7"
+			echo "Unsupported KERNEL_FLAVOUR, please specify one of: wb2, wb6, wb7, sa02m, sa02m-rt"
 			return 1
 	esac
 
